preConditionHook:
// EL: avgRange = average(high - low, rangeLookback)[1] -- the mean bar range
// over the rangeLookback bars ending ONE BAR AGO, so the breakout bar is not
// in its own benchmark. The indexed-Average idiom LargeOutsideBar uses.
//
// Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808),
// and high - low is a price expression with real history, so this is a FRESH
// loop over price -- not the WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator and not a
// mirrored variable buffer. Summed newest-first, EL's Summation order.
//
// The condition is kept whole rather than split into a body-fraction rule and
// a range-vs-average rule: neither half stands alone in the source, and the
// pair is the book's single named 'strong breakout bar'. Direction-agnostic --
// AbsValue of the body, so a bear breakout bar passes on both sides.
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    avgRange += high[1 + i] - low[1 + i];
}
avgRange /= (int)rangeLookback;
